   "he": "מָה יְהֵא בַּדָּמִים? רַבִּי טַרְפוֹן אוֹמֵר יִשְׁתַּמֵּשׁ וְכוּ׳. עַד כָּאן לָא פְּלִיגִי",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «What shall be» done «with the money» received from the sale of the animal? «Rabbi Tarfon says:» The finder «may use it;» therefore, if the money is lost, he is liable to pay restitution for its loss. Rabbi Akiva says: He may not use the money. Therefore, if it is lost, he is not liable to pay restitution. The Gemara analyzes the tannaitic dispute: Rabbi Tarfon and Rabbi Akiva «disagree»"
  }
